Algorithm: Biomedical Equipment Maintenance and Fault Management System

1. Start the program.
2. Load existing equipment records from the data file.
3. Display the menu containing registration, listing, searching, fault management, status updates, maintenance scheduling, priority sorting, and report generation.
4. Read the user's menu choice.
5. Perform the selected operation:

   A. Register Equipment
   - Read equipment ID, name, department, status, fault description, and maintenance date.
   - Check that the ID is unique and the date is valid.
   - Store the equipment details in the array.
   - Save the records to the data file.

   B. List Equipment
   - Traverse the equipment array using a loop.
   - Display all equipment details and maintenance status.

   C. Search Equipment
   - Accept an equipment ID or name.
   - Search the array using a linear search.
   - Display matching records or a not-found message.

   D. Manage Faults
   - Search for equipment using its unique ID.
   - Record the fault description and update the fault status.
   - Mark equipment with a newly recorded fault as out of service.
   - Save the updated record.

   E. Update Equipment Status
   - Find the equipment by ID.
   - Update its operational status.
   - Mark its fault as resolved when it is explicitly returned to operational status.
   - Save the changes.

   F. Schedule Maintenance
   - Find the equipment by ID.
   - Accept and validate the next maintenance date.
   - Update and save the schedule.

   G. Sort by Priority
   - Calculate a priority score for each equipment record.
   - Assign higher scores to overdue maintenance, open faults, and out-of-service status.
   - Sort the records in descending priority using bubble sort.
   - Display the sorted records.

   H. Generate Reports
   - Traverse all equipment records.
   - Count overdue maintenance, open faults, and out-of-service equipment.
   - Display the maintenance and fault report.

6. Return to the menu unless the user chooses Exit.
7. Terminate the program.

End.
